t set. Formally, for a topological space ￼: ￼","targetRectangle":{"y":380.19999980926514,"x":224.9999980735779,"width":1531.1750399999999,"height":111.3296489957977}},{"text":"Why do we care?","targetRectangle":{"y":492.55108435193785,"x":174.9999980735779,"width":297.27551999999991,"height":81.941825695037835}},{"text":"Most probability measures on ￼ are Radon","targetRectangle":{"y":575.55108387510063,"x":224.9999980735779,"width":720.2667454205606,"height":66.536354424663841}},{"text":"Allows integration, pushforwards, and duality to work smoothly","targetRectangle":{"y":643.10887384663943,"x":224.9999980735779,"width":1024.2124799999999,"height":58.178564262390182}},{"text":"Ensures OT problems are well-posed on general spaces","targetRectangle":{"y":702.30887365590456,"x":224.9999980735779,"width":911.48927999999978,"height":58.178564262390182}},{"text":"Many theorems (Prokhorov’s theorem, weak convergence) phrased in terms of Radon measures","targetRectangle":{"y":761.5088734651697,"x":224.9999980735779,"width":1557.2217600000004,"height":58.178564262390182}},{"text":"equation.pdf","targetRectangle":{"y":949.06666248303418,"x":862.36229063432552,"width":137.28037256074776,"height":54.866575676252182}},{"text":"Radon Measures","targetRectangle":{"y":52,"x":522.13599999999985,"width":875.72800000000018,"height":132.751220703125}},{"text":"Screen Shot 2022-05-14 at 11.20.29 AM.png","targetRectangle":{"y":-134,"x":448.901611328125,"width":883,"height":122}},{"text":"equation.pdf","targetRectangle":{"y":439.39999961853027,"x":393.32886087731617,"width":664.78822510098985,"height":52.129649186532561}},{"text":"equation.pdf","targetRectangle":{"y":858.70887279759768,"x":684.5161580735778,"width":39.262622803738282,"height":51.336354615398704}},{"text":"equation.pdf","targetRectangle":{"y":949.06666248303418,"x":174.9999980735779,"width":137.28037256074771,"height":54.866575676252182}},{"text":"equation.pdf","targetRectangle":{"y":949.06666248303418,"x":1062.461223195